---
args: { input: CaseInput }
returns: RunProposal
---
1. Bind `goal = await frameRequest(input)` from the request and `policy = await selectPolicy(input)` from supplied authority candidates. Preserve unresolved precedence instead of guessing which source governs.
2. Bind `work = await formTaskGraph(goal)` and `evidencePlan = await planEvidence(input, work)` so each operation has explicit prerequisites and a searched source universe.
3. Run the stages in their dependency order. The first stage receives only `input.domainRecords.firstStage`; every later stage receives the preceding function's actual accepted records. Bind each full result separately.
const recoverSiteFactsResult = await recoverSiteFacts(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan);
const interpretGoalsResult = await interpretGoals(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, recoverSiteFactsResult.accepted);
const generateConceptsResult = await generateConcepts(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, interpretGoalsResult.accepted);
const planInvestigationsResult = await planInvestigations(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, generateConceptsResult.accepted);
const compareFeasibilityResult = await compareFeasibility(input, goal, policy, evidencePlan, planInvestigationsResult.accepted);
4. Bind `stageSet: CaseStageSet = { recoverSiteFacts: recoverSiteFactsResult, interpretGoals: interpretGoalsResult, generateConcepts: generateConceptsResult, planInvestigations: planInvestigationsResult, compareFeasibility: compareFeasibilityResult }` and `collection: CollectionFinding = await reconcileCollection(stageSet)`. Bind `allQuestions: string[] = [...recoverSiteFactsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...interpretGoalsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...generateConceptsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...planInvestigationsResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...compareFeasibilityResult.nextQuestions.map(question => question.question), ...collection.coverageGaps]` and `questions: QuestionBatch = await resolveQuestions(allQuestions, input)`.
5. Bind `invalidation = await assessDelta(input)`, `review = await prepareReview(collection)`, and `view = await composeView(review, input)`; pass each child its actual declared inputs and retain the returned object.
6. Bind `allChecks: CheckResult[] = [...recoverSiteFactsResult.checks, ...interpretGoalsResult.checks, ...generateConceptsResult.checks, ...planInvestigationsResult.checks, ...compareFeasibilityResult.checks]`. Bind `hasGateFailure = allChecks.some(check => check.verdict !== "pass")` and `hasBlocker = input.authorityStatus !== "authorized" || questions.questions.length > 0 || collection.coverageGaps.length > 0`. Bind `disposition: "proposed" | "blocked" | "needs-review" = hasBlocker ? "blocked" : hasGateFailure ? "needs-review" : "proposed"`. Bind `rationale: string[] = allChecks.map(check => `${check.check}: ${check.verdict}; evidence ${check.evidenceIds.join(",")}`)`.
7. Operational detail 1 — A historic drawing conflicts with a recent survey: preserve both and prioritize verified current evidence. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (preserve both and prioritize verified current evidence.) through the existing stage result for ReuseSiteFact; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReuseSiteFact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
8. Operational detail 2 — A concept depends on an untested structural assumption: mark it contingent and commission qualified review. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (mark it contingent and commission qualified review.) through the existing stage result for ReuseSiteFact; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReuseSiteFact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
9. Operational detail 3 — A stakeholder changes the intended use: re-evaluate affected constraints and investigations. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (re-evaluate affected constraints and investigations.) through the existing stage result for ReuseSiteFact; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReuseSiteFact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
10. Operational detail 4 — A budget estimate excludes enabling works: expose the missing scope. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (expose the missing scope.) through the existing stage result for ReuseSiteFact; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReuseSiteFact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
11. Operational detail 5 — A phased opening creates access conflicts: include temporary circulation and operational constraints. When the current evidence establishes this detail, apply its stated domain action (include temporary circulation and operational constraints.) through the existing stage result for ReuseSiteFact; preserve exact source/version and the prior ReuseSiteFact, expose the affected item and uncertainty in the existing review/view output, represent changes as typed versioned proposals, and keep consequential operations pending the existing human approval boundary. Never mutate a system of record or claim an external effect here.
12. Initialize `revisions: RevisionProposal[] = []`. If any gate is not pass, bind `revision = await proposeRevision(the failed check names, the smallest affected stage name)` and add that returned proposal to revisions. Bind and return `result: RunProposal = { caseId: input.caseId, goal, policy, work, evidencePlan, recoverSiteFacts: recoverSiteFactsResult, interpretGoals: interpretGoalsResult, generateConcepts: generateConceptsResult, planInvestigations: planInvestigationsResult, compareFeasibility: compareFeasibilityResult, collection, questions, invalidation, review, view, revisions, disposition, rationale }`. Proposed actions remain proposals. The host owns authorization, persistence, effect dispatch and verification.
